            <ArticleTitle>Intraocular coccidioidomycosis simulating a neoplasm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>218-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bjo.2011.202515</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coccidioidomycosis can simulate an intraocular neoplasm. We reviewed a case report of a 10-year-old girl who was referred with an intraocular tumour. This tumour consisted of a coccidioidomycosis infection in the eye. The eye was blind and painful so it was removed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
